# repo-audit-skills architecture

Git catalog of **Cursor skills and agents** for repository audits. Installed via [ide-agents](https://github.com/sergeychernov/ide-agents) as symlinks (Global or Project).

## Layout

```
repo-audit-skills/
├── skills/
│   └── <skill-name>/
│       ├── SKILL.md
│       ├── scripts/          # optional — bundled helpers
│       └── assets/           # optional — markers, checklists
└── agents/                   # optional — *.md subagent personas
```

Nested layout only: `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Flat root layout is not used here.

## Audit context in target repos

Skills write runtime context into the **audited project**, not into this catalog:

```
<target-repo>/
└── .audit/
    ├── profile.json          # stack profile (audit-init)
    └── reports/              # *.json reports (gitignore optional)
```

Downstream skills **read** `.audit/profile.json` first; they do not re-detect the stack. All `.audit/` artifacts are **JSON only** — see `audit-artifacts.mdc`. JSON Schemas stay in `skills/*/assets/`, not in `.audit/`.

## Scope conventions

| Skill kind | Typical `scope` |
|------------|-------------------|
| `audit-init`, dimension audits | `project` — context lives in target repo |
| Generic reviewers | `any` or `global` |

Project-scoped installs symlink into `<target>/.cursor/skills/`.

## Principles

- Scripts are read-only auditors by default — no code changes in the target repo.
- No network calls, no `node_modules` access in scan scripts.
- Deterministic output: same repo state → same profile/findings.
- Generic tooling only — no corporate or private audit criteria in this repo.
